WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.742
ALEX: Okay. Claude Ship. Let's actually
explain what this is, because the name

00:00:02.742 --> 00:00:05.483
ALEX: does not tell you.

00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:09.112
JAMIE: The name sounds like a logistics
startup that failed in 2019.

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:14.394
ALEX: Heh. So — Anthropic released this
on November twenty-third. It's a suite

00:00:14.394 --> 00:00:19.565
ALEX: of three AI agents built
specifically around GitHub pull
requests. Code Review

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:24.737
ALEX: is generally available. PR Steward
and Claude Approvals are both in beta.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:27.535
RUFUS: And the distinction between those
three matters enormously.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.134
ALEX: Tell me.

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:32.868
RUFUS: Code Review analyses your code —
that's the familiar part, AI as

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:37.491
RUFUS: reader. PR Steward goes one step
further: it handles merge conflicts,
pushes

00:00:37.491 --> 00:00:42.115
RUFUS: fixes, responds to feedback. But
it cannot actually approve a merge.
